    "id": "p31-q64-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "64",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-\\dfrac{8y}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}$, $x\\ne6y,-2y$.\n\nFactorise and cancel within each fraction, then subtract using a common denominator.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac{x-6y}{(x-6y)(x+2y)}-\\frac{x-6y}{(x-6y)^2}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac1{x+2y}-\\frac1{x-6y}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=\\frac{(x-6y)-(x+2y)}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}\\\\\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-4xy-12y^2}-\\frac{x-6y}{x^2-12xy+36y^2}&=-\\frac{8y}{(x+2y)(x-6y)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne6y$ and $x\\ne-2y$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
